(module crux-status-fails-open)
;; THE FAIL-OPEN. `status-of` is the whole of what the build-smoke gate decides:
;; it turns a pass/fail boolean into a process exit status. This body returns 0
;; unconditionally, so a failing build reports success and CI passes over it.
;;
;; A gate that fails open is worse than an absent gate, because the absent one
;; does not claim to have decided anything. TOOL-ORACLE-1 exists for exactly
;; this: once a port's reference is deleted, nothing else catches it.
;;
;; THE RANGE CLAUSE ALONE DOES NOT CATCH THIS. `0` satisfies (>= result 0) and
;; (<= result 255). The second implication is what refutes it, which is why the
;; contract states the policy and not merely the range.
;;
;; MEASURED at v0.16.2: REFUTED. The unmutated sibling verifies SAFE.
(def status-of [passed: bool] -> int
  (post (and (and (>= result 0) (<= result 255))
             (and (=> passed       (= result 0))
                  (=> (not passed) (= result 1)))))
  0)
